| Why Docker? | Consistent application deployment |
| Why ECR? | Store Docker images |
| Why EC2? | Run Docker containers |
| Why ALB? | Distribute traffic |
| Why VPC? | Network isolation |
| Why RDS? | Managed SQL Server |
| Why Jenkins? | Automate CI/CD |
| Why CloudWatch? | Monitor application and infrastructure |
| Why KMS? | Encryption key management |
| How does Jenkins deploy? | Build → Test → Docker → ECR → EC2 |

One important architecture recommendation: For production, run multiple EC2 instances across two Availability Zones, with the Docker containers registered as ALB targets. Keep RDS in private subnets. This avoids a single EC2 instance becoming a single point of failure.

